# Staging areas

## A landing zone between source & warehouse

- Holds the **raw output of extract**, mirroring the source
- Schema-light, uninterpreted · transform reads **from here**

## Why it earns its place

- **Decouples** extract from transform → **source released** fast
- **Safe workspace** — clean/conform without touching source or warehouse
- **Restart checkpoint** — re-run transform without re-extracting
- **Raw audit copy** — reprocess after a logic fix; prove what arrived

## Transient or persistent

- **Transient** — truncate & reload each run (working buffer)
- **Persistent** — keep every extract (raw archive, ~DV raw layer)

## ETL vs ELT

- ETL: staging in the engine · ELT: **raw tables in the warehouse**
